            <ArticleTitle>Barodontalgia at 12,000 feet.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Persons susceptible to barodontalgia include those with peridontal abscesses, carious teeth, maxillary sinus congestion, or those who have had recent extractions or restorations. A 38-year-old man had acute pain while he was in a depressurized chamber. Treatment of a periodontal abscess alleviated the problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
